WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.880
A ratio of three to two means three equal parts of one

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.310
thing for every two equal parts of another.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.090
The numbers three and two are not the amounts.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.330
They count parts.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.810
Find the size of one part, and everything else follows.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.150
Ratios run through recipes, maps,

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.950
mixtures and sharing problems.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.990
Nearly all of them are solved by the same step:

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.950
work out what one part is worth.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.590
Forty stickers are shared between Ana and Ben in the

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:28.980
ratio three to two.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.580
How many does each get?

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.220
Pause and count the parts.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.180
There are three plus two parts: five altogether.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.470
Forty stickers in five equal parts is eight per part.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.500
Ana gets three parts, twenty-four.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.220
Ben gets two parts, sixteen.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.410
The given fact is not always the total.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.380
Suppose instead you are told that Ana has nine

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.040
more than Ben.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.110
Ana has one more part than Ben, so one part is nine.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.210
Then Ana has twenty-seven and Ben has eighteen.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.530
To join two ratios, make the shared quantity match.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.610
If A to B is two to three, and B to C is four to five,

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.390
rewrite both so that B is twelve parts.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.090
Then A to B to C is eight to twelve to fifteen.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.800
Ratios and fractions are two views of one picture.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.430
In the ratio three to two, the first share is three

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.910
fifths of the whole, not three halves and

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:28.720
not two thirds.

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:30.800
Count the parts.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.310
Use what you are told, a total, a difference or one

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.080
share, to find one part.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:36.920
Then multiply.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.550
Notebook challenge: red and blue beads are in the ratio

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:43.980
five to three, and there are sixteen more red than blue.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:45.900
How many beads are there altogether?
